# PyTorch CPU-Only Docker Image – Docker Lab

## Project Overview

This project focuses on building and running a CPU-compatible Docker image for the xFusionCorp Industries ML platform team.

The provided Dockerfile contained an incorrect PyTorch package index targeting GPU wheels and a default command that required CUDA availability. Since the lab environment provides CPU-only hardware, these settings prevented the container from meeting the required specifications.

The Dockerfile was updated to install PyTorch from the official CPU wheel index and execute a startup command that displays the installed PyTorch version and CUDA availability.

## Objectives

- Inspect and repair the existing Dockerfile.
- Configure PyTorch installation using the CPU-only wheel index.
- Build the Docker image with the required tag.
- Configure a CPU-compatible default container command.
- Verify successful container execution.
- Confirm that CUDA availability returns `False`.

